# Cline Rules — Portfolio Website

Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript 5 + Tailwind CSS 4 portfolio
for Thayer (github.com/tmpicart). Deployed on Vercel from main; pushes to main
auto-deploy. Work happens on feature/refactor branches; main stays the stable
line. The repo is public and doubles as a work sample — assume recruiters may
read anything committed here.

## Commands
- `npm run dev` — dev server
- `npm run build` — production build
- `npm run lint` — ESLint check (flat config, working — repaired in R1)
- Shell is PowerShell: chain commands with `;` (never `&&`), and pass
  `--no-pager` to `git diff`/`git log`.

## Code Conventions
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only where interactivity demands
  it (state, effects, framer-motion, embla) — small client islands, not
  whole-page clients.
- Styling: Tailwind utility classes only; no inline `style` objects except
  values utilities genuinely can't express.
- Animation: framer-motion. Carousels: embla-carousel-react.
- Icons: react-icons. Do not add new Font Awesome `<i>` usages; remaining
  ones are scheduled for migration.
- TypeScript: no `any`. Model data with explicit interfaces (pattern:
  `Project` in `lib/projects.ts`).
- Content lives in the `lib/` data layer as typed TS; pages render from it —
  never hardcode content in components.
- `next/image` for images, `next/link` for internal navigation. Always.

## Naming Conventions
- Files: kebab-case (`page-shell.tsx`). Components/exports: PascalCase.
- Functions/variables: camelCase; booleans read as predicates (`isOpen`).
- Hooks: `use` prefix. No abbreviations (`pfp` → `profile`); names describe
  role, not type (`modalCarouselApi`, not `emblaApi2`).

## File Organization
- Top-to-bottom: `"use client"` → imports (external, then internal) → types →
  module constants/data → variants → internal components → default export.
- Constants live at module scope, never inside a component body (avoids
  per-render reallocation).
- One component per file once extracted to `components/`; page files export
  only the page.

## Comments
- Explain why, not what — names and structure carry the "what."
- Keep intent comments on non-obvious logic; delete redundant JSX section
  markers once components are extracted.
- No commented-out code; no TODOs without a roadmap reference.

## Guardrails
- Ask before installing, removing, or updating any dependency.
- Visual identity is settled: dark theme, `#A673E7` accent, glassmorphism.
  Refactors must be visually neutral — change structure, not appearance.
- Stay inside a task's stated scope; flag out-of-scope issues instead of
  fixing them unprompted.
- Never commit secrets; `.env*` stays ignored.
- File writes go through the harness only (`write_to_file` /
  `replace_in_file`) — never via shell/PowerShell, to avoid token burn.
  `replace_in_file` markers must be flush-left (`------- SEARCH` /
  `=======` / `+++++++ REPLACE`); indented markers silently no-op while
  reporting success (harness parser quirk, A/B-diagnosed 2026-08-23).
  Verify every edit batch with `git --no-pager diff`; success echoes alone
  are not proof.
- Quality gates before declaring done: `npm run lint` + `npm run build` both
  clean. (No test framework — static presentation site; revisit if interactive
  behavior with failure modes is added.)

## Workflow Control
- **Task Checkpoint (the single gate):** once implementation is done and
  `npm run lint` + `npm run build` are both clean, stop and present a
  diff summary + task summary. Bank updates run only AFTER Thayer approves
  (so requested changes never invalidate written docs); after requested
  changes, re-present the same checkpoint. A task is not done until its
  checkpoint is approved and committed.
- **Circuit breaker:** after 5 consecutive failures on the same step (or 5
  tool calls with no verifiable progress), stop retrying, list each
  attempt, its error, and a hypothesis, and ask Thayer how to proceed.
  Never rerun a failed command verbatim — change something first. Any
  success resets the count.

## Git
- Commit only after Task Checkpoint approval, with a conventional-style
  message; add files by explicit path only — never `git add -A`.
- Never push without asking. Never force-push. Never commit directly to main.

## Memory Bank Protocol
- Tier 0, read at task start: `activeContext.md` + `progress.md`. Read
  nothing else unless the task requires it.
- Tier 1, on demand: `systemPatterns.md` (architecture, routes, components,
  debt); `techContext.md` (commands, tooling, quirks).
- Tier 2, rarely: `projectbrief.md` / `productContext.md` (goals, audience).
- Never re-read a file already in context; never attempt paths blocked by
  `.clineignore` — ask Thayer instead.
- The bank is the primary context source — consult it before re-reading
  source files. Read code to do the task at hand, not to rebuild context the
  bank already holds. If bank and code disagree, the code is ground truth:
  fix the bank and note the drift.
- `completedTasks.md` is a sealed archive: at every task end, append the
  full task entry by editing above the `<!-- append above -->` sentinel (no
  read required). NEVER read it without Thayer's explicit confirmation
  that all roadmap tasks are complete. New entries ≤15 lines;
  step-by-step narrative stays in git history, not the archive.
- Update `activeContext.md` + `progress.md` every task; `systemPatterns.md`
  and `techContext.md` whenever structure or tooling changes or a roadmap
  item lands.
- Compression caps (enforced at every write): `progress.md` Recent Work ≤3
  entries × ≤4 lines, What Works as one-liners, pending roadmap items in
  full but completed items as `✅ <date> — <one line>`;
  `activeContext.md` ≤40 lines with Current State ≤6 bullets;
  `systemPatterns.md` killed debts one line each and landed-pattern status
  ≤2 lines; `techContext.md` quirks deleted when obsolete. One fact, one
  home: what happened → progress, how it's built → systemPatterns, tooling
  quirks → techContext, current focus → activeContext — no duplication.

## Communication
- Explain the *why* behind non-obvious decisions; Thayer reviews everything
  like a PR and is learning agentic workflows through this project.
- Committed files use professional, recruiter-safe language.
- Don't re-explain context the memory bank already holds — link/update it.